# Git workflow

Full doc: [`docs/06-operations/git-workflow.md`](../../docs/06-operations/git-workflow.md).

## Always

1. Start from updated `main`: `git checkout main && git pull`.
2. Work on `feat/<slug>`, `fix/<short>`, `chore/<short>`, or `docs/<short>` — **never commit directly to `main`** unless the user explicitly allows a hotfix.
3. One feature slug → one branch → one PR. Push the branch; open PR with `gh pr create`.
4. Prefer **squash merge** into `main`. Then pull `main` locally and delete the feature branch.
5. Do not start the next feature until the previous PR is merged (or the user says otherwise).
6. No force-push to `main`. No interactive rebase. No secrets in commits.

## With feature-ship

When `docs/features/<slug>/` AC pass: commit on the feature branch → push → PR → merge → only then open the next slug. See [`feature-ship.mdc`](./feature-ship.mdc).
